uce Sarah's contribution now, referencing James's recommendation and perhaps adding nuance.\n\nWe need to decide Sarah's vote. According to shared mental model, Sarah currently has no vote. She can either agree with B or propose another candidate. Let's evaluate: She might have concerns about B's communication style. She might consider Candidate C's crew cooperation and decision quality. But C has egocentric and communication difficulty. D has responsibility but moody. A has leadership but unorganized and not good at criticism.\n\nGiven the evidence, B still seems strongest. Sarah could agree with James, but perhaps raise the communication concern more strongly, and suggest mitigation. She could still vote B.\n\nThus produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE: agree with James, note B's strengths, mention communication concerns, propose mitigation, and maintain vote for B.\n\nMETADATA_JSON: {\"agent\":\"sarah_mitchell\",\"vote\":\"Candidate B\"}\n\nMake sure to follow format: PUBLIC_MESSAGE: then content, then METADATA_JSON.\n\nLet's craft concise argument."}
